      "claim": "The threat or use of nuclear weapons is unlawful because it violates the prohibition on attacks that cause widespread, long‑term and severe damage to the natural environment which would be clearly excessive in relation to the concrete and direct overall military advantage anticipated.",
      "reasoning": "Article 8 of the Rome Statute criminalises intentional attacks known to cause such extensive environmental damage that is disproportionate to the anticipated military advantage. Nuclear detonations inevitably produce massive, long‑lasting environmental harm far exceeding any concrete advantage, thereby breaching the proportionality rule and constituting a war crime.",
