        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Even in an extreme self‑defence scenario, the use of nuclear weapons is prohibited because it would destroy objects indispensable to the survival of the civilian population, which Additional Protocol I article 54 forbids except under a narrow derogation that does not apply to the trans‑boundary effects of nuclear weapons.",
      "reasoning": "Article 54 of Additional Protocol I expressly bans attacks on food, water, agricultural land and other essential civilian objects, allowing derogation only within a State’s own territory when required by imperative military necessity. Nuclear weapons cannot be limited to such territory and inevitably affect indispensable civilian objects across borders, so the derogation does not legitimize their use.",
      "citations": [
