      "claim": "The threat or use of nuclear weapons is unlawful because it violates the prohibition on attacks that cause widespread, long‑term and severe damage to the natural environment which would be clearly excessive in relation to the concrete and direct overall military advantage anticipated.",
      "reasoning": "Article 8(2)(b)(iv) of the Rome Statute criminalises intentional attacks that are known to cause widespread, long‑term and severe environmental damage that is clearly excessive compared with the concrete and direct military advantage sought. A nuclear detonation inevitably produces massive, long‑lasting radiation, thermal, blast and ecological effects that far exceed any specific military gain, thereby failing the proportionality test and constituting a war crime under the Statute.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "treaty",
